=== Def 9.4.

The exponent $e(G)$ of a finite group $G$ is the least integer $e>0$ such that $a^e=1$ forall $a in G$.
The exponent $e(U_n)$ is called the universal exponent of $n$, denoted by $e(n)$.

By Lagrange's theorm $e(G)| abs(G)$ so $e(n)|phi(n)$.

=== Lemma 9.5

The exponent of product of cyclic groups is the lcm of their orders.

