=== Theorem 9.7 (Korselt)

If $n$ is a Carmichael number, then $n$ is a square-free and $p-1$ divides $n-1$ for each $p$ dividing $n$.

==== Pf.

If $n$ is a Carmichael, then by def $a^(n-1)equiv 1 mod n, forall a in ZZ$.\
So $e(n)|(n-1)$.
If $p^f||n$, then $e(n)$ is divisible by $e(p^f)$\
$e(p^f)=phi(p(f))=p^(f-1)(p-1)$, so $p-1|n-1$.
If $f>1$, then $p|n-1$ as well.
But this is impossible since $p|n$.
Hence $f$ is at most $1$.

